# Shared checkout · clean worktree

**Invariant:** `shared_attended_checkout ⇒ branch ∈ {master, current_unchanged}` · `needs(feature_branch ∨ review_branch ∨ land_isolate) ⇒ git worktree add (clean)` · `¬git checkout(other_branch) on the shared tree` · `sole_maintainer_local ⇒ ¬push ∧ ¬pr` unless the operator names push / PR / publish · `forward_only ⇒ ¬move(shared_branch, backward)`.

Switching the shared tip for side work steals it from peer WIP. "Submit for review" ⇒ local branch + `git diff --stat <base>..HEAD`, ¬ `git push` / `gh pr create`. `¬ stash` to free the tip.

## Detents

- Tip already not `master`: ¬ force-switch mid-turn unless named; ¬ switch further for new side work — worktree from the start-point.
- Trivial same-tip edit on the current shared branch: stay; worktree optional.
- `lane=B`: substrate worktrees suffice; ¬ move the shared IDE checkout.

## Land (attended)

```
shared tip stays master → worktree -b land/<slug> → commit → merge into master → remove worktree
```

No-PR removes the remote step, ¬ the worktree.

| Bad | Good |
|---|---|
| Switch the shared tip to a side branch, amend, switch back | `git worktree add` and work there |
| Push or open a PR because a brief said "submit for review" | Local `@sha` + diffstat; land when told |

